 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The Spirit, who kept not them under,\nSaw the flame of Death's soul come into\nHimself and set them on fire,\nAnd made his own a son, dying\nLike one whose glory would decay,\nHad he none. This was their Maker,\nTheir light; nor was it just before\nDeath that they should be asked therefore,\nThat He might not kill Himself\nFor all things so far too heavy\nHe neither could, nor thought to suffer,\nNor yet had pity enough",
